<!--
    Add to res/values/styles.xml, and use style="@style/PluginButton" on EVERY
    button in the plugin.

    The SDK template already copies ATAK's own button drawables out of the SDK:
    btn_gray is a selector over new_dark_button_bg / _selected / _disabled —
    black-to-#383838 gradient, #585858 border, green border when pressed, flat
    grey when disabled. Do not invent a button background; a plugin that looks
    like ATAK is a plugin an operator can already use.

    ATAK's own darkButton sets vertical padding only, which lets a short label
    render wider than its own background. This adds horizontal padding and a
    44dp minimum height — a touch target for a gloved hand on a vehicle mount,
    not a cosmetic choice.

    Put no textSize on the widget itself or it fights the style.
-->
<style name="PluginButton" parent="@style/darkButton">
    <item name="android:paddingLeft">12dp</item>
    <item name="android:paddingRight">12dp</item>
    <item name="android:paddingTop">6dp</item>
    <item name="android:paddingBottom">8dp</item>
    <item name="android:minHeight">44dp</item>
    <item name="android:minWidth">0dp</item>
    <item name="android:textSize">15sp</item>
    <item name="android:singleLine">true</item>
    <item name="android:ellipsize">end</item>
</style>
